  "label": "Textual claim mapped onto visual scene",
  "description": "The text 'little foil on top keeps them jewsy' is mapped onto the visual scene of the brick oven, implying that the contents inside (presumably human remains) are being 'kept' or preserved by foil, which is a grotesque antisemitic stereotype. This mapping uses the visual of the oven to represent the Holocaust and the foil to symbolize a false, dehumanizing explanation for Jewish identity.",
